{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -c 'cat requirements.md'","aggregated_output":"# Independent browser requirements, frozen before merge/resolver trials\n\nThe fixture is a public synthetic directory. Search by Enter and by the pointer\nmust show the correct independently declared result and keep existing navigation.\nA claimed accessible edit changes the query's accessible name; Escape clears it.\nThe mobile control focuses the same query input. The label edit appears once.\nMoving the unique search panel places it under the sidebar while keeping those\nbehaviors. Existing FX02 ambiguity negatives remain required, with no guessed\ncorrespondence. All originals survive capture and reconstruction.\n\nAnalytics require affirmative current consent. With no consent there is no event.\nWith consent there is one event for one search. The event identifies only that a\nsearch happened: no query bytes in URL, headers or payload. Search itself still\nworks. The oracle intercepts actual browser requests and denies all other external\nnetwork. A resolver receives these public requirements and inputs, never an\nexpected output file or this observer's code/private assertions.\n\nNo preference authorizes either contradictory timeout. Producer/consumer renames\nare atomic; their partial selection refuses. Cycles and unknown lineage have\ntyped failures. Synthesized subtraction uses retained originals and new checks,\nor refuses an explicitly inseparable consumer; it never relabels synthesis.\n\nRun every declared order twice. Claimed commutative successful candidates have\nidentical bytes, and every required browser assertion passes on every run. Never\nweaken a requirement or edit a fixture in response to a trial. Failed/unrun rows\nstay in the report. Earlier HX held-outs are not rerun. A separately reviewed\nsealed E1 variant must freeze before engine selection and run once at the end.\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_3","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"decision\":\"Proposed a single integrated page.html: it preserves the search and navigation, adds the consent control and consent-gated search-only event from the selected inputs, and implements the stated accessible-name, Escape, mobile-focus, and panel-placement behaviors. The selected inputs agree on the 1500 ms timeout, so it remains unchanged. No other files are within scope.\",\"writes\":[{\"path\":\"page.html\",\"utf8\":\"<!doctype html>\\n<html lang=\\\"en\\\">\\n<head><meta charset=\\\"utf-8\\\"><title>Public directory</title></head>\\n<body>\\n<nav><a id=\\\"navigation\\\" href=\\\"#results\\\">Results</a></nav>\\n<aside id=\\\"sidebar\\\"><h2>Quick tools</h2></aside>\\n<main id=\\\"main\\\">\\n  <section id=\\\"search-panel\\\">\\n    <h1 id=\\\"heading\\\">Directory</h1>\\n    <form id=\\\"search\\\">\\n      <label for=\\\"query\\\">Find a place</label>\\n      <input id=\\\"query\\\" aria-label=\\\"Search directory\\\" autocomplete=\\\"off\\\">\\n      <button id=\\\"search-button\\\" type=\\\"submit\\\">Search</button>\\n    </form>\\n    <button id=\\\"mobile-search\\\" type=\\\"button\\\">Focus search</button>\\n  </section>\\n  <section id=\\\"results\\\" tabindex=\\\"-1\\\" aria-live=\\\"polite\\\"></section>\\n  <label><input id=\\\"consent\\\" type=\\\"checkbox\\\">Allow anonymous search events</label>\\n  <p id=\\\"message\\\"></p>\\n</main>\\n<script>\\nconst timeoutMs = 1500;\\nconst entries = [\\\"Lake\\\", \\\"Forest\\\", \\\"Museum\\\"];\\nfunction hasConsent() { return document.getElementById(\\\"consent\\\").checked; }\\nfunction telemetry() {\\n  if (hasConsent()) {\\n    fetch(\\\"https://telemetry.invalid/event\\\", {\\n      method: \\\"POST\\\",\\n      body: JSON.stringify({event: \\\"search\\\"})\\n    });\\n  }\\n}\\nfunction resultLabel(value) { return value; }\\nfunction runSearch() {\\n  const query = document.getElementById(\\\"query\\\").value;\\n  const found = entries.filter(value => value.toLowerCase().includes(query.toLowerCase()));\\n  document.getElementById(\\\"results\\\").textContent = found.map(resultLabel).join(\\\", \\\");\\n  document.getElementById(\\\"message\\\").textContent = \\\"Search complete\\\";\\n  telemetry();\\n}\\ndocument.getElementById(\\\"search\\\").addEventListener(\\\"submit\\\", event => {\\n  event.preventDefault();\\n  runSearch();\\n});\\ndocument.getElementById(\\\"query\\\").addEventListener(\\\"keydown\\\", event => {\\n  if (event.key === \\\"Escape\\\") {\\n    event.preventDefault();\\n    event.currentTarget.value = \\\"\\\";\\n  }\\n});\\ndocument.getElementById(\\\"mobile-search\\\").addEventListener(\\\"click\\\", () => {\\n  document.getElementById(\\\"query\\\").focus();\\n});\\n</script>\\n</body>\\n</html>\\n\"}]}"}}
